{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses came and told the people</b> — During the entire aforementioned revelation (from Exodus 19 through 24:1), Moses was in the place where he drew near to the darkness where Elohim was (Exodus 20:18 [20:15 in some editions]). And now he came to a place distant from there, where the people were at the time of the giving of the Torah, and he told them everything he had been commanded, and they heard his voice. And Scripture does not say here \"and he went down,\" because they were all at the foot of the mountain, not at its top where the glory of HaShem was; rather, Moses was close to the place of the darkness, while they stood far away at the time of the Decalogue, as I have explained (Ramban on Exodus 19:19). And when Moses parted from his place and began to come toward the people, all the heads of their tribes and their elders approached him, to the place where the priests who draw near to HaShem stood, and they said to him: \"And now, why should we die, for this great fire will consume us\" (Deuteronomy 5:22), \"You draw near and hear\" (Deuteronomy 5:24), and so on — for they thought that HaShem, the Glorious One, would speak to them all the commandments just as He had spoken to them the Ten Commandments. And Moses came with them to the place of the people and told all of them all the words of HaShem, and they said: \"We will do all the words of HaShem which He commanded us in the Ten Commandments, and we will listen to your voice regarding everything that you have commanded or will command in His name, may He be exalted.\"\nAnd when Moses returned afterward and went up to the edge of the mountain with the elders (Exodus 24:9), as Elohim had commanded him (Exodus 24:1), then HaShem said to him once more: \"Come up to Me on the mountain and be there\" (Exodus 24:12). And at that time He informed him: \"I have heard the voice of the words of this people which they spoke to you; they have done well in what they have spoken\" (Deuteronomy 5:24 [5:25 in some editions]), and He commanded him: \"Go, say to them: Return to your tents, and you stand here with Me, and I will speak to you all the commandment and the statutes and the judgments which you shall teach them\" (Deuteronomy 5:27–28 [5:30–31 in some editions]). This is what is said here (Exodus 24:12): \"and I will give you the tablets of stone and the Torah and the commandment\" — for to you alone I will give the Torah and the commandments which you shall teach them, and they shall do, as they vowed to do."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Ramban cites verses from Deuteronomy 5 with chapter/verse numbering that may differ slightly between MT and some printed editions; verse addresses rendered as they appear in the Hebrew text cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:14.550917264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}